WEBVTT

00:00:00.750 --> 00:00:02.750
Gyokuto
Private
High
School

00:00:02.450 --> 00:00:07.500
As you can see, on the surface,
it looks like a normal high school.

00:00:10.910 --> 00:00:14.910
When off base, both of you be sure
to act as if that's the case.

00:00:15.790 --> 00:00:18.500
There really is no one here, is there?

00:00:18.660 --> 00:00:22.040
Um, that's called "camouflage," right?

00:00:22.040 --> 00:00:24.200
Huh? Then, the base...

00:00:24.660 --> 00:00:26.580
I seem to recall going underground...

00:00:28.200 --> 00:00:29.120
Underground?

00:00:30.910 --> 00:00:31.830
If you don't mind.

00:00:32.450 --> 00:00:33.500
Understood.

00:00:38.000 --> 00:00:41.120
Y-yeah. This is what happened!

00:00:41.200 --> 00:00:43.330
It's become an elevator, huh?

00:00:50.750 --> 00:00:51.830
This way.

00:00:51.830 --> 00:00:53.580
This is the base?

00:00:53.580 --> 00:00:55.120
Yeah. Probably.

00:01:03.160 --> 00:01:04.790
Welcome...

00:01:11.500 --> 00:01:14.160
To the Mondenkind iDOL team!

00:01:18.620 --> 00:01:21.290
Miss Amami. Miss Hagiwara.

00:01:21.830 --> 00:01:23.830
We shall be counting on you.

00:01:26.540 --> 00:01:27.620
Sir!

00:01:27.250 --> 00:01:29.620
I've heard the S.O.S.

00:01:29.620 --> 00:01:34.580
Have you finally heard it?

00:01:48.120 --> 00:01:50.540
In a cutesy way

00:01:50.540 --> 00:01:54.080
Impure or pure, which character?

00:01:54.080 --> 00:01:56.910
Maybe they're the same

00:01:56.910 --> 00:01:59.450
The love beat is opened up full throttle

00:01:59.790 --> 00:02:04.450
I've noticed, this is a special mission... I've got it

00:02:05.330 --> 00:02:10.870
I'll show you for real, because I'll make it come true

00:02:10.870 --> 00:02:14.750
In a world that's pierced through the skies

00:02:15.700 --> 00:02:21.660
I felt a strange emotion, I liked you in an instant!

00:02:24.540 --> 00:02:26.750
I'm sure I'll win with a smile

00:02:26.750 --> 00:02:30.080
Sure enough a smile is the right way

00:02:30.080 --> 00:02:35.660
I was small and crying but I'll rise to the challenge

00:02:35.660 --> 00:02:38.000
I wonder what this palpitation is

00:02:38.000 --> 00:02:41.290
I need a little medical attention

00:02:41.290 --> 00:02:49.370
This feeling of slight fever
could be your fault, S.O.S!

00:02:58.620 --> 00:03:03.790
iDOL and Master

00:02:58.910 --> 00:03:05.330
Thus, following Lost Artemis,
we have supported the Earth in secret.

00:03:05.660 --> 00:03:08.870
We must devote ourselves to our duties,

00:03:08.870 --> 00:03:11.790
never forgetting that we support
the livelihoods of others.

00:03:12.040 --> 00:03:13.330
Sir!

00:03:13.580 --> 00:03:14.830
Very good.

00:03:14.830 --> 00:03:16.080
Now, I would like to
introduce the members.

00:03:16.080 --> 00:03:17.580
So long!
Now, I would like to
introduce the members.

00:03:17.580 --> 00:03:18.950
Upperclassman!
First, Naze Munakata. And Sorewa Suzuki.

00:03:18.950 --> 00:03:22.410
First, Naze Munakata. And Sorewa Suzuki.

00:03:23.080 --> 00:03:24.370
Naraba Daido.

00:03:25.160 --> 00:03:29.620
These three are in charge of
base administration.

00:03:29.620 --> 00:03:30.950
Very nice to meet you!

00:03:30.950 --> 00:03:32.160
Nice to meet you.

00:03:32.450 --> 00:03:34.450
N-nice to meet you.

00:03:35.080 --> 00:03:37.000
Ah. Also, Miss Naze.

00:03:37.000 --> 00:03:38.160
Huh?! Sir!

00:03:38.500 --> 00:03:41.620
Please send a report to HQ for me.

00:03:41.700 --> 00:03:43.700
C-come on!

00:03:44.660 --> 00:03:47.660
Japan Branch duties are one day a week.

00:03:47.660 --> 00:03:51.580
On that day, you're usually
on standby for Drops.

00:03:52.120 --> 00:03:53.330
Drops?

00:03:53.330 --> 00:03:56.080
Konpeito that fall down to Earth.

00:03:56.200 --> 00:03:58.080
Oh, those!

00:03:58.410 --> 00:04:01.200
In my hometown,
we just called them meteorites.

00:04:02.500 --> 00:04:03.950
Now, first off...

00:04:04.450 --> 00:04:05.870
This is the locker room.

00:04:04.660 --> 00:04:07.660
Kikuchi
Minase

00:04:06.540 --> 00:04:08.830
Use those two at the end there.

00:04:09.410 --> 00:04:11.120
And this is the training room.

00:04:11.830 --> 00:04:12.790
Your sleeping quarters.

00:04:17.450 --> 00:04:20.080
We have a Japanese-style room too,
thanks to the director's tastes.

00:04:20.080 --> 00:04:21.620
What would we use it for?

00:04:21.620 --> 00:04:22.750
Beats me...

00:04:24.450 --> 00:04:26.660
And this is the shower room.

00:04:28.750 --> 00:04:30.830
Ah, perfect timing.

00:04:31.330 --> 00:04:33.160
This is your upperclassman.

00:04:33.620 --> 00:04:36.750
Iori Minase. These two are-

00:04:36.750 --> 00:04:38.080
I know.

00:04:40.330 --> 00:04:41.700
I thought I told you:

00:04:41.700 --> 00:04:43.580
You can't handle Imber.

00:04:44.580 --> 00:04:45.870
Um...

00:04:46.660 --> 00:04:48.080
Not that it matters, but...

00:04:48.700 --> 00:04:50.700
That's a rather daring pose.

00:05:10.500 --> 00:05:11.540
Beginning activation.

00:05:14.290 --> 00:05:16.040
Imber activation confirmed.

00:05:16.040 --> 00:05:17.620
Output is increasing.

00:05:17.620 --> 00:05:23.200
Will reach stable levels in
80... 70... 60... 50...

00:05:24.290 --> 00:05:25.870
Output has stopped increasing.

00:05:26.120 --> 00:05:27.370
And core readings?

00:05:28.620 --> 00:05:31.660
Normal. Silicon dendrites are stable.

00:05:32.250 --> 00:05:34.410
It would seem the Imber is active.

00:05:34.410 --> 00:05:37.910
What are your thoughts as
the Imber's head mechanic?

00:05:38.160 --> 00:05:40.620
I can't find any mechanical problems.

00:05:41.250 --> 00:05:44.120
It must be compatibility between
the iDOL and master.

00:05:44.620 --> 00:05:46.080
Good enough?

00:05:46.620 --> 00:05:50.290
If I couldn't get it to move, it'll NEVER move.

00:05:50.540 --> 00:05:51.870
You sound pretty confident.

00:05:51.870 --> 00:05:53.000
It's a fact.

00:05:53.000 --> 00:05:55.500
But Haruka made it move.

00:05:55.870 --> 00:05:59.330
She didn't MAKE it move.
It just happened to move.

00:06:03.580 --> 00:06:05.500
She's an Idolmaster too.

00:06:06.080 --> 00:06:07.790
Miss Makoto Kikuchi.

00:06:08.250 --> 00:06:10.370
She's your upperclassman.

00:06:11.790 --> 00:06:14.750
V-very nice to meet you.

00:06:14.750 --> 00:06:16.040
Yeah, hi.

00:06:17.540 --> 00:06:20.330
Well, shall we start your training?

00:06:20.500 --> 00:06:23.540
Training? So, we ride this?

00:06:23.750 --> 00:06:25.290
One day.

00:06:26.700 --> 00:06:28.700
But before then...

00:06:27.500 --> 00:06:31.290
Drop Countermeasures
for Beginners

00:06:29.370 --> 00:06:32.200
THIS comes first?

00:06:31.290 --> 00:06:32.870
( 3 ) Maple Belt

00:06:32.660 --> 00:06:40.200
So, the Drops' danger is determined not
just by their size but by their angle of entry.

00:06:32.870 --> 00:06:35.250
( 2 ) Honey Belt
( 1 ) Sugar Belt

00:06:40.250 --> 00:06:43.120
Thus, Question 1 in your textbook, Yukiho...

00:06:43.120 --> 00:06:44.080
Yes?

00:06:44.080 --> 00:06:45.950
What is the degree of danger in this case?

00:06:45.950 --> 00:06:48.500
Ma'am. Well, using this formula...

00:06:50.040 --> 00:06:51.040
It's a Mint Drop.

00:06:51.040 --> 00:06:55.500
Generally, they burn up in the atmosphere
without having to be dealt with.

00:06:55.660 --> 00:07:01.040
Correct. We deploy to take care of
Drops graded Lemon and above.

00:07:01.750 --> 00:07:04.540
Drops are traditionally
eliminated with missiles,

00:07:04.540 --> 00:07:07.580
but because Japan can't possess
weapons of mass destruction,

00:07:07.660 --> 00:07:10.500
we use iDOLs to deal with them.

00:07:10.790 --> 00:07:14.080
Thus, our country is
the only one to have iDOLs-

00:07:14.080 --> 00:07:15.160
Um...

00:07:15.660 --> 00:07:18.120
Um, Haruka appears to be somewhat...

00:07:18.910 --> 00:07:21.450
Haruka? Is something the matter? Haruka!

00:07:26.160 --> 00:07:29.160
Ah! Haruka! Are you all right?

00:07:29.160 --> 00:07:29.830
Come to think of it,

00:07:29.830 --> 00:07:30.120
Hang in there!
Come to think of it,

00:07:30.120 --> 00:07:30.910
Hang in there!
her math and science grades
in middle school were catastrophic, huh?

00:07:30.910 --> 00:07:33.000
Hello? Haruka!
her math and science grades
in middle school were catastrophic, huh?

00:07:33.000 --> 00:07:35.700
Are you all right? Haruka!
her math and science grades
in middle school were catastrophic, huh?

00:07:37.330 --> 00:07:39.500
This seems like it could be worthwhile...

00:07:40.540 --> 00:07:42.870
It's five hundred million!
Five hundred million!

00:07:42.870 --> 00:07:43.370
Now, now.
It's five hundred million!
Five hundred million!

00:07:43.750 --> 00:07:47.870
Do you know how hard it was
to raise that kind of money?!

00:07:47.910 --> 00:07:52.040
Our president personally held meetings
and had the country pay half that amount,

00:07:52.040 --> 00:07:55.870
so where does your boss
get off not even showing up?!

00:07:55.870 --> 00:07:57.620
Now, now.

00:07:57.620 --> 00:07:59.790
For now, let's address the issue.

00:08:01.290 --> 00:08:06.620
Uh, here is what the Geneva
Disciplinary Committee has decided:

00:08:06.910 --> 00:08:13.200
"The Mondenkind Japan iDOL Team
will continue acting as at present.

00:08:13.200 --> 00:08:16.370
"Their leader, Joseph Shingetsu,
will be reprimanded."

00:08:16.370 --> 00:08:17.160
What?!

00:08:17.160 --> 00:08:20.120
He gets a reprimand for all THAT?!
How ridiculous!

00:08:20.120 --> 00:08:23.830
Again? Why is HQ so soft on these guys?

00:08:23.830 --> 00:08:25.790
I refuse to accept this!

00:08:25.790 --> 00:08:27.120
Now, now.
I refuse to accept this!

00:08:27.160 --> 00:08:29.410
Well, I'll just be going...

00:08:29.410 --> 00:08:32.830
Wait there! I'm not through talking!

00:08:32.830 --> 00:08:36.580
Indeed. We'd like a written letter
of apology for this.

00:08:37.000 --> 00:08:40.870
Let's see... About 100 of them for Geneva.

00:08:40.870 --> 00:08:42.080
But... Why...?
Let's see... About 100 of them for Geneva.

00:08:42.080 --> 00:08:42.620
But... Why...?
And an additional 100 for...

00:08:42.620 --> 00:08:43.910
But... Why...?

00:08:50.410 --> 00:08:52.450
It came up from here?

00:08:53.620 --> 00:08:55.410
Hard to understand, huh?

00:08:56.750 --> 00:09:03.870
I thought it would never move again.
Is that kid so special?

00:09:04.290 --> 00:09:06.250
The Prince of the Moon...

00:09:14.950 --> 00:09:16.500
Um...

00:09:16.620 --> 00:09:17.700
What should I...?

00:09:23.330 --> 00:09:27.580
Don't get worked up about it.
First, master each individual movement.

00:09:28.160 --> 00:09:29.370
Ma'am.

00:09:40.370 --> 00:09:41.250
All right!

00:09:47.580 --> 00:09:51.120
Haruka, that's amazing.
I couldn't do it at all.

00:09:52.040 --> 00:09:55.120
I've always been good at this kind of thing.

00:09:55.120 --> 00:09:57.080
Even my brother couldn't
beat me at video games.

00:09:57.410 --> 00:10:00.200
Haruka, you might be suited for this.

00:10:00.540 --> 00:10:07.200
That's not true at all. I've only just started,
and I didn't get that Drop study at all!

00:10:07.370 --> 00:10:09.450
But that was so good!

00:10:10.000 --> 00:10:10.910
Really...?

00:10:10.950 --> 00:10:12.250
Yes!

00:10:13.830 --> 00:10:15.000
A blackout?

00:10:16.330 --> 00:10:17.660
We've restored it.

00:10:17.910 --> 00:10:20.160
Confirming lost data.

00:10:21.330 --> 00:10:25.950
This is no good, either?
What do you think, Forehead?

00:10:26.160 --> 00:10:29.580
Nothing I think matters!
It won't move an inch!

00:10:29.620 --> 00:10:31.580
Did you really do maintenance on this?

00:10:31.580 --> 00:10:33.000
Of course I did!

00:10:33.000 --> 00:10:37.250
Data condition is exactly
the same as the Nebula.

00:10:37.250 --> 00:10:38.450
What's going on?

00:10:38.450 --> 00:10:39.120
Oh, sorry!

00:10:39.120 --> 00:10:44.290
We thought this could be our chance, so
we tried applying load to the Imber, but...

00:10:44.290 --> 00:10:46.950
This chick said she wanted to do it.

00:10:46.950 --> 00:10:49.200
Ch-Chikako! How cruel!

00:10:49.700 --> 00:10:53.950
Well, it's her first time as lead mechanic.
Let's overlook this.

00:10:54.790 --> 00:10:55.830
So that's it.

00:10:56.000 --> 00:10:59.200
Ma'am! That's not it at all!
Chikako made me-

00:10:59.200 --> 00:11:00.620
And how did it turn out?

00:11:00.620 --> 00:11:02.080
U-um...

00:11:06.500 --> 00:11:07.620
Haruka.

00:11:08.080 --> 00:11:09.080
Ma'am?

00:11:09.080 --> 00:11:10.290
Wanna give it a spin?

00:11:10.580 --> 00:11:11.250
Huh?!

00:11:11.700 --> 00:11:14.450
How much longer will it take to get it ready?

00:11:14.450 --> 00:11:19.330
How much longer? It'll take time to look into
what just happened, so two days...

00:11:19.330 --> 00:11:23.330
Do it in one day, please.
And I'll keep it from the boss.

00:11:23.950 --> 00:11:25.660
Out of options, huh?

00:11:25.660 --> 00:11:27.160
You'd better help me.

00:11:27.620 --> 00:11:29.080
Okay, by tomorrow.

00:11:34.200 --> 00:11:35.370
Huh?

00:11:36.250 --> 00:11:40.500
That's why you have to do
club activities with this kid, huh?

00:11:40.750 --> 00:11:44.450
Yeah. But this whole time,
the kid hasn't moved...

00:11:44.450 --> 00:11:50.580
I mean, hasn't come to school,
so I wonder if I can even be a pilot.

00:11:50.580 --> 00:11:51.290
"Pilot"?

00:11:51.290 --> 00:11:56.080
Uh, no, no! Um, I wonder if
we can even SPEAK to each other.

00:11:56.700 --> 00:11:59.950
I see. You've had it rough, Haruka.

00:12:00.000 --> 00:12:01.080
Uh, yeah.

00:12:01.500 --> 00:12:03.580
Still, it's been kinda fun, right?

00:12:03.660 --> 00:12:04.540
Huh?!

00:12:04.580 --> 00:12:08.040
I can kind of get it. Hearing your voice.

00:12:09.080 --> 00:12:10.540
Really?

00:12:10.700 --> 00:12:15.500
Well, you just do what you like, right?
I'll be here to talk to you whenever.

00:12:16.660 --> 00:12:20.830
Yeah. Thanks. Okay, I'll call you tomorrow.

00:12:23.370 --> 00:12:26.620
Is it fun? I wonder...

00:12:34.620 --> 00:12:38.290
Um... Is it okay like this?

00:12:38.540 --> 00:12:40.540
It really suits you!

00:12:40.540 --> 00:12:42.200
R-really?

00:12:42.200 --> 00:12:45.080
They just seem like workout clothes...

00:12:45.080 --> 00:12:46.750
Incredible.

00:12:47.080 --> 00:12:52.540
Haruka, you suddenly have to do this,
but you're not nervous at all.

00:12:52.700 --> 00:12:56.290
Uh, it's not as if I'm NOT nervous.

00:12:56.950 --> 00:12:59.750
But, it's like...

00:13:00.790 --> 00:13:02.500
Well, whatever!

00:13:03.160 --> 00:13:04.330
"Well, whatever"?

00:13:04.660 --> 00:13:05.660
Yeah.

00:13:07.000 --> 00:13:10.910
I can't explain it very well, but-

00:13:11.370 --> 00:13:14.750
Haruka Amami, please head for the hangar.

00:13:14.950 --> 00:13:15.370
Repeating: Haruka Amami,
please head for the hangar.

00:13:15.370 --> 00:13:16.500
Oh. I have to go.
Repeating: Haruka Amami,
please head for the hangar.

00:13:16.500 --> 00:13:17.580
Repeating: Haruka Amami,
please head for the hangar.

00:13:17.580 --> 00:13:19.500
Yes. Please do your best.
Repeating: Haruka Amami,
please head for the hangar.

00:13:20.750 --> 00:13:22.250
Okay, let's begin.

00:13:23.040 --> 00:13:25.120
Well? How does the cockpit feel?

00:13:25.120 --> 00:13:28.370
Somehow, I can't relax. But I'll be okay.

00:13:28.580 --> 00:13:29.830
Probably.

00:13:29.950 --> 00:13:33.870
It will be the same as the simulator.
You remember that, right?

00:13:34.040 --> 00:13:36.870
Yes! I think I'll be fine.

00:13:37.500 --> 00:13:38.870
All right, here goes.

00:13:38.870 --> 00:13:42.700
Hmph! There's no way that new chick
could make it move.

00:13:43.290 --> 00:13:45.080
First, the activation.

00:13:45.290 --> 00:13:48.620
All right! Um, first off...

00:13:58.120 --> 00:13:59.830
Imber activation is confirmed.

00:14:00.040 --> 00:14:05.500
Output levels rising.
Will reach stable levels in 80... 70...

00:14:05.500 --> 00:14:06.830
60...

00:14:06.830 --> 00:14:07.910
50...

00:14:07.910 --> 00:14:11.000
40... 30... 20...

00:14:11.000 --> 00:14:12.120
10!

00:14:15.080 --> 00:14:16.790
H-huh?

00:14:28.750 --> 00:14:30.750
Protective barriers No. 2 and 5 activated!

00:14:30.950 --> 00:14:34.450
Abort the test!
Release the silicon dendrites!

00:14:49.910 --> 00:14:52.040
What? What was that?

00:14:52.160 --> 00:14:54.120
Haruka? Haruka!

00:14:54.330 --> 00:14:56.290
Uh, yes.

00:14:56.580 --> 00:14:57.620
You all right?

00:14:57.620 --> 00:15:01.370
Yes. I'm fine. Um, what was...?

00:15:01.870 --> 00:15:05.200
Sorry. Would you mind
staying put for a bit?

00:15:05.450 --> 00:15:06.080
Huh?

00:15:06.080 --> 00:15:09.410
Can I be blunt? You've been sealed up.

00:15:09.450 --> 00:15:11.660
You're confined. CON-FINED.

00:15:12.120 --> 00:15:13.700
N-no way!

00:15:13.700 --> 00:15:15.660
We're finding out what happened.

00:15:15.870 --> 00:15:18.000
Do you know anything on your end?

00:15:18.200 --> 00:15:23.290
My end? Lots of things flashed
and disappeared on the monitors...

00:15:23.290 --> 00:15:24.370
And now?

00:15:24.370 --> 00:15:26.540
Now, there's nothing.

00:15:29.450 --> 00:15:31.000
Inorganic Crystalline Lifeform Embryology Team B,

00:15:31.000 --> 00:15:32.700
Mondenkind AUS says it will be another
60 before their work shift.
Inorganic Crystalline Lifeform Embryology Team B,

00:15:32.700 --> 00:15:34.870
Mondenkind AUS says it will be another
60 before their work shift.
head for No. 6 Conference Room.

00:15:34.870 --> 00:15:35.370
Switch Extraterrestrial Intelligence
Probe program F to…

00:15:35.370 --> 00:15:37.000
What about the Imber?
Switch Extraterrestrial Intelligence
Probe program F to…

00:15:37.500 --> 00:15:39.250
It's not looking good.

00:15:39.450 --> 00:15:43.290
Then it can't be helped.
Suspend special shift.

00:15:43.290 --> 00:15:48.160
The Imber will remain on standby as-is.
Chikako, how is the Nebula?

00:15:48.750 --> 00:15:50.410
Good to go whenever.

00:15:50.790 --> 00:15:53.910
Sir, Iori Nagase is entering the ready room.

00:15:54.080 --> 00:15:55.120
It's time.

00:15:55.700 --> 00:15:59.870
Commence work shift. Mondenkind Japan
will begin Drop monitoring.

00:16:01.660 --> 00:16:02.700
All right!

00:16:03.040 --> 00:16:05.410
They better show up today! Drops!

00:16:11.620 --> 00:16:13.450
Sure am hungry...

00:16:15.750 --> 00:16:17.450
Hey.

00:16:18.370 --> 00:16:20.950
HEY, Mr. Imber!

00:16:24.620 --> 00:16:27.330
I guess I'm no good after all...

00:16:29.870 --> 00:16:31.160
What is this?

00:16:34.250 --> 00:16:37.040
What? You want to tell me something?

00:16:40.580 --> 00:16:41.540
Yes?

00:16:41.660 --> 00:16:43.250
Ah, Haruka?

00:16:43.250 --> 00:16:48.120
I'm done with work, so I thought we could
go eat or something. It's on me!

00:16:48.450 --> 00:16:50.450
Sorry. I can't today.

00:16:50.540 --> 00:16:53.160
What's wrong? You sound gloomy.

00:16:53.250 --> 00:16:54.000
Yeah...

00:16:54.200 --> 00:16:57.620
Oh, I know. It's that kid you were
talking about yesterday.

00:16:57.620 --> 00:16:59.250
Things didn't go well, huh?

00:16:59.330 --> 00:17:00.660
"Well"?

00:17:01.120 --> 00:17:04.160
Yeah. Looks like it didn't go well.

00:17:04.330 --> 00:17:05.870
Haruka?

00:17:07.290 --> 00:17:10.160
Are you thinking about way back then?

00:17:10.250 --> 00:17:10.950
Huh?

00:17:11.040 --> 00:17:13.410
You're too kind, Haruka.

00:17:15.410 --> 00:17:18.700
You can't be so easy on people.
Like the old you.

00:17:21.450 --> 00:17:25.200
The old... me?

00:17:25.700 --> 00:17:28.330
Doing it by force should be just right.

00:17:28.330 --> 00:17:31.410
There are different ways
to go about it, but...

00:17:32.120 --> 00:17:37.200
At the very least, I'VE used
that way to make a good friend.

00:17:39.000 --> 00:17:40.370
Yayoi...

00:17:42.200 --> 00:17:43.910
Huh? What's that sound?

00:17:43.950 --> 00:17:48.750
Ah, sorry! Things are getting crazy here.
I'll call you later.

00:17:48.870 --> 00:17:50.250
Hey, wait!

00:17:50.370 --> 00:17:52.290
The Drop is a confirmed Lemon!

00:17:52.290 --> 00:17:54.290
Nebula, stand by to deploy.

00:17:55.660 --> 00:17:57.290
All right, let's go!

00:17:58.040 --> 00:18:01.120
Say, Imber? Maybe I...

00:18:01.830 --> 00:18:05.660
I think I understand you a little.

00:18:05.660 --> 00:18:09.000
So would you... spend time
with me for a bit?

00:18:09.450 --> 00:18:11.250
Huh? Wait just a moment!

00:18:12.040 --> 00:18:12.910
Are you serious?

00:18:12.910 --> 00:18:16.500
Yes. I'm sure he's scared.

00:18:16.790 --> 00:18:21.620
He's been inside this whole time,
and when he finally goes out,

00:18:21.620 --> 00:18:24.080
he was surprised by what happened,
and got scared.

00:18:24.250 --> 00:18:28.500
His hands and legs are frozen.
He wants to move but he can't.

00:18:29.040 --> 00:18:33.000
But no matter how much he's told
"It's all right," his fear won't go away!

00:18:33.580 --> 00:18:36.910
Not until he goes outside
and makes sure for himself.

00:18:38.120 --> 00:18:39.950
She's a fun girl...

00:18:40.370 --> 00:18:42.540
Switch the Imber to Channel 26.

00:18:42.870 --> 00:18:44.200
For real?!

00:18:44.700 --> 00:18:47.040
That's all right, sir?

00:18:47.540 --> 00:18:53.120
Of course. This is the thrill of the iDOLs.
It sets the heart racing.

00:18:53.120 --> 00:18:56.040
Let's do our best to fulfill
those expectations.

00:18:57.790 --> 00:19:00.120
Switching Imber to Channel 26.

00:19:00.330 --> 00:19:01.870
I'll have to write more letters of apology...

00:19:01.870 --> 00:19:06.120
Miss Naze. Should something go wrong,
the letters of apology, if you please.

00:19:06.120 --> 00:19:07.200
Bingo!

00:19:07.700 --> 00:19:08.660
Yeah, thanks.

00:19:17.950 --> 00:19:19.160
You're sending out the Imber?

00:19:19.620 --> 00:19:22.910
Give me a break! That thing's
never moved properly!

00:19:23.160 --> 00:19:25.790
The Nebula will devote itself
to Drop elimination.

00:19:25.790 --> 00:19:27.500
We'll take care of recovery.

00:19:27.540 --> 00:19:29.750
I was gonna do that without you telling me!

00:19:32.080 --> 00:19:34.580
Nebula cleared for Routes 5 through 13.

00:19:34.790 --> 00:19:37.290
Haruka. You're ready, right?

00:19:37.450 --> 00:19:38.290
Yes!

00:19:38.790 --> 00:19:41.040
Nebula, deploy!

00:19:44.750 --> 00:19:46.080
Got it?

00:19:46.080 --> 00:19:48.910
All we can do is launch the Catapult.

00:19:49.000 --> 00:19:50.660
After that, it's up to you.

00:19:50.700 --> 00:19:54.200
You'll be fine. If it doesn't work,
we'll still land you in the ocean.

00:19:58.790 --> 00:20:02.660
It's not scary. I'm all right. It's not scary.

00:20:05.120 --> 00:20:06.450
Let's go, Imber!

00:20:22.080 --> 00:20:24.950
Imber. Don't be scared.

00:20:25.450 --> 00:20:26.450
Take a good look.

00:20:26.660 --> 00:20:27.700
It's the ocean.

00:20:30.000 --> 00:20:32.700
See? Those are konpeito.

00:20:33.750 --> 00:20:36.410
Nothing to be afraid of.
This feels good, right?

00:20:36.830 --> 00:20:38.750
The Imber is losing altitude.

00:20:39.040 --> 00:20:41.160
It will hit the ocean's surface in 20 seconds!

00:20:41.500 --> 00:20:43.410
Ready a recovery vessel.

00:20:44.660 --> 00:20:47.580
It's all right. I'm not scared.

00:20:48.000 --> 00:20:53.500
You know, when you make a scary face,
everyone else makes scary faces.

00:20:55.580 --> 00:21:00.120
But if you smile, everyone
will show you THEIR smiles.

00:21:01.370 --> 00:21:05.080
That's it. That's all there is to it.

00:21:05.160 --> 00:21:06.580
Another 10 seconds.

00:21:07.120 --> 00:21:09.790
So, let's fly.
8, 7, 6, 5, 4, 3, 2, 1...

00:21:09.790 --> 00:21:10.450
8, 7, 6, 5, 4, 3, 2, 1...

00:21:10.450 --> 00:21:12.250
Imber! Let's fly!
8, 7, 6, 5, 4, 3, 2, 1...

00:21:13.950 --> 00:21:16.080
Fly! With me!

00:21:31.660 --> 00:21:32.660
Imber!

00:21:33.370 --> 00:21:36.410
The Imber is active!
Output has reached stable levels!

00:21:36.700 --> 00:21:38.870
It is under the Idolmaster's control!

00:21:39.660 --> 00:21:40.750
It's like a dream!

00:21:44.790 --> 00:21:46.580
Emergency signal from the Nebula!

00:21:55.120 --> 00:22:04.080
Like a saint that crosses the ages

00:22:04.080 --> 00:22:13.040
In what kind of loneliness did you cry?

00:22:13.040 --> 00:22:21.910
Stretching out to a star so far away

00:22:21.910 --> 00:22:30.450
Say, I'll depict my feelings, look up at the sky

00:22:32.080 --> 00:22:41.910
Dear boy, if I always look for you in my heart

00:22:41.910 --> 00:22:50.870
Ah, I'll release a light so strong it will envelop you

00:22:50.870 --> 00:22:59.830
That sparkling trail will be the guide for us both

00:22:59.830 --> 00:23:11.410
Now, no matter where we look, we feel the truth

00:23:24.750 --> 00:23:39.750
Preview
Pot Stickers and Corndogs

00:23:27.000 --> 00:23:28.370
Why do you better yourself?

00:23:28.370 --> 00:23:30.120
To be Nebula's pilot.

00:23:30.120 --> 00:23:31.450
Why do you get angry?

00:23:31.450 --> 00:23:33.330
To encourage myself.

00:23:33.330 --> 00:23:35.080
Why does your forehead shine?!

00:23:35.080 --> 00:23:37.000
Ah! Well...

00:23:37.000 --> 00:23:39.500
To illuminate the world with love!
